From 3530de360986961705d5c07627f70f9d20d4ed96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:15:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-snd: bound the wait for the microphone, refuse a
 denied permission early, stop capture units off the control thread

Upstream steamac's 0024 (STEAMAC-8N/8P) moved capture into a worker with a
200 ms START deadline, a microphone-permission check and a RELEASE that
returns buffers while the HAL is stuck. This fork's 0018/0020/0022/0023/0030
already answer START at once and open the microphone on a per-stream start
worker (and 0025 records from a VR headset), so 0024 itself does not apply;
this ports its three behaviours onto that design:

- The guest's capture I/O waits for the microphone at most 200 ms after
  START (CAPTURE_START_WAIT). Before, it waited for as long as the start
  worker did: a permission prompt or a stuck HAL left arecord without data
  until it timed out. After 200 ms the pump delivers clock-paced silence (as
  for a missing device) until the unit runs; the late open is logged once.
- The start worker asks AVCaptureDevice for the microphone permission first.
  Denied or restricted fails the start at once, without any HAL call (whose
  start can wait on TCC), and capture gets paced silence; "undetermined" goes
  on and lets macOS ask. The input device and the permission are logged.
- A capture unit taken off its stream (STOP, RELEASE, a new START, a VR
  headset switch) is no longer stopped by the caller: the stream's worker
  stops it, in order and before it opens the next one (StartGate::kick). The
  control thread called AudioOutputUnitStop itself, so a stuck HAL hung STOP
  and RELEASE with the guest's queued buffers.

Upstream state: steamac 1.9.15's 0024 (not applied in this fork, see
host/libkrun/build.sh). Tests (fail without this patch):
capture_waits_for_the_microphone_at_most_the_start_bound,
denied_microphone_permission_fails_the_start_without_the_hal,
capture_stop_and_release_do_not_wait_for_a_stuck_unit_stop,
start_gate_tests::a_kick_runs_the_worker_once_more_without_a_request.
